  "doc": {
    "description": "11 -- SRLatch: state from cross-coupled gates, with defined power-on.\n\nFeedback is well-defined in SHDL's unit-delay model (§11.2): every\ngate recomputes once per cycle from last cycle's values, so a wire\nmay depend on its own previous value.  Cross-coupled NORs therefore\nhold state with no special syntax.\n\nThe init block seeds chosen nets at cycle 0 (§11.4) -- it produces no\ngates, only power-on metadata.  Here the latch comes up reset (Q = 0)\ninstead of relying on the all-zeros default, which would briefly be\ninconsistent (Q = Qn = 0) until the loop settles.",
    "source": "circuit.shdl",
